      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T16:08:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Have you thought about using build/make/tools/generate-notice-files.py instead? I\u0027m okay with adding this one because generate-notice-files.py will probably add an additional step in your use case, though. If you decide to keep this script, please consider adding a comment about its limited use case, i.e. should not be used for the final output, and using the same duplicate check logic as generate-notice-files.py\u0027s.",
      "revId": "ada834ced39317817d2a7502856af4e03d95df86",
