    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d982de4a_128041e2",
        "filename": "scripts/mergenotice.py",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060667
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T16:31:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, this got me thinking, if you merge all notice files here, generate-notice-files.py won\u0027t be able to detect duplicates because it relies on notice file paths. How about making LOCAL_NOTICE_FILE hold a list of notice file paths and letting generate-notice-files.py handle all merge actions instead?",
      "parentUuid": "9124c60a_dc331e12",
      "revId": "ada834ced39317817d2a7502856af4e03d95df86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "455a76cf_26b72f68",
        "filename": "scripts/mergenotice.py",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T16:47:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah I did, but that one critically assumes that input NOTICE files are all found in the same directory, which can\u0027t be true for our case. I could amend the script to accept input files as positional parameters, but it will only complicate the script without giving much benefit.\n\nIn addition, I don\u0027t think the duplicate check routine should be the same. set() used here is good enough to detect duplicate. I frankly think the use of md5 hash in the script is a little bit overkill.\n\nI\u0027ve update the comment.\n\n---------------\nFor the second comment:\n\nTo generate-notice-files.py, individual files inside an APEX aren\u0027t visible. It only sees a big APEX having multiple licenses.\n\nIt looks like you want to reveal them all, which I don\u0027t think necessary. We don\u0027t do that for other packing formats like APK either.",
      "parentUuid": "9124c60a_dc331e12",
      "revId": "ada834ced39317817d2a7502856af4e03d95df86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a59907e5_8fa8d5fb",
        "filename": "scripts/mergenotice.py",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060667
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T17:03:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e To generate-notice-files.py, individual files inside an APEX aren\u0027t visible. It only sees a big APEX having multiple licenses.\n\nNot sure if I\u0027m following you here. What I\u0027m suggesting is ditching this and just outputting all notice file source paths in the bundle\u0027s LOCAL_NOTICE_FILE. (Which will require you to make notice_files.mk handle multiple paths in a single LOCAL_NOTICE_FILE.) That way, generate-notice-files.py will be able to see all notice files and merge them correctly.",
      "parentUuid": "455a76cf_26b72f68",
      "revId": "ada834ced39317817d2a7502856af4e03d95df86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "76d75740_950f3ce0",
        "filename": "scripts/mergenotice.py",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-20T22:59:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "generate-notice-files.py associates a module and its license file by looking at $(PRODUCT_OUT)/obj/NOTICE_FILES/src directory. If there is a file system/foo/bar/file.ext.txt under the directory then the file is assumed to be the license file for system/foo/bar/file.ext\n\nSince what we are installing is a big APK, not individual files in it, $(PRODUCT_OUT)/obj/NOTICE_FILES/src/system/apex/com.android.xxx.apex.txt should be the notice file for the APEX. We can\u0027t have multiple notice files for the single APEX... because path to the file encodes the associated file on the device.\n\nDan, do you have any comment? I thought this is what you suggested.",
      "parentUuid": "a59907e5_8fa8d5fb",
      "revId": "ada834ced39317817d2a7502856af4e03d95df86",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
